+### Step 2 — release and install task-board `0.25.0`
+
+Repository/version: `skill-project-management 0.25.0`, exact public
+agents-management `v0.5.0`. agents-infra remains the old installed release.
+
+Required board capability: the saved current-pair remains able to perform all
+spawn/route/resource/CR operations. Before install, the reviewed candidate runs
+the full suite/build, graph inventory, binary symbol inventory and an
+out-of-place real spawn-and-review canary. After install, repeat the same live
+canary through installed `task-board`.
+
+Required install command and pre-window preconditions:
+
+```bash
+set -euo pipefail
+RECOVERY_ROOT="$HOME/.local/state/TASK-260830-s5ro4e/current-pair"
+PM_RELEASE="$HOME/.local/state/TASK-260830-s5ro4e/release-candidates/skill-project-management-0.25.0"
+PM_SAVED_SOURCE="$RECOVERY_ROOT/sources/skill-project-management"
+test "$(git -C "$PM_RELEASE" describe --tags --exact-match)" = "0.25.0"
+
+# Outside the window: every environment override the release reads is
+# classified, install_skills is unchanged from the source this section was
+# derived against, and every dependency skill is already a real directory so the
+# installer cannot take its network clone branch inside the window.
+require_env_overrides_classified "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh" \
+  classify_pm_env_override
+require_mirrored_function_unchanged "$PM_SAVED_SOURCE/scripts/setup.sh" \
+  "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh" install_skills
+require_mirrored_function_unchanged "$PM_SAVED_SOURCE/scripts/setup.sh" \
+  "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh" write_install_state
+require_mirrored_function_unchanged "$PM_SAVED_SOURCE/scripts/setup.sh" \
+  "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh" install_roles
+require_mirrored_function_unchanged "$PM_SAVED_SOURCE/scripts/setup.sh" \
+  "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh" register_skill
+require_dependency_skills_materialized "$PM_RELEASE"
+derive_pm_setup_stages "$PM_RELEASE" > "$RECOVERY_ROOT/w2-stages.txt"
+
+# The window opens here. A bare machine-scoped install is mandatory: no flag is
+# permitted, because --configure-project additionally enables configure_project,
+# check_agents_infra_compose and bootstrap_local_agents inside the same window
+# and writes a project task-board.config.json this plan does not model.
+env -u TASK_BOARD_PROJECT_DIR -u TASK_BOARD_CONFIGURE_PROJECT \
+    -u TASK_BOARD_BOOTSTRAP_LOCAL_AGENTS -u TASK_BOARD_MODE -u TASK_BOARD_DIR \
+    -u TASK_BOARD_REMOTE -u TASK_BOARD_USER -u TASK_BOARD_ID \
+    -u TASK_BOARD_TLS_NO_VERIFY -u TASK_BOARD_SETUP_SOURCE_ONLY \
+  "$PM_RELEASE/scripts/setup.sh"
+```
+
+The `env -u` list is exactly the `unset` disposition of
+`classify_pm_env_override`, and `require_env_overrides_classified` fails the
+step when the release reads an override the classification does not cover, so
+the two cannot drift apart silently.
+
+In-flight runs: provider children and already-exec'd CLI/sessiond processes
+continue. A run that reaches a new CLI mutation during the mixed window may see
+a partial default install; retry its mutation through the recovery-prefixed old
+pair. Do not reparent, rewrite or kill the run. An interruption inside
+`install_skills` leaves a managed skill tree or one of its two links in a
+partial state; recovery authority for that surface is
+`restore_managed_skills_from_snapshot`, run as part of the Step-2 rollback, and
+the run is not resumed until the rollback canary is green.
+
+Mixed-install window `W2`: opens at the first `install_binary` call and closes
+only when installed verification plus the live canary succeeds, or when rollback
+plus the recovery canary succeeds. The stages inside it are not restated here;
+they are the sequence `derive_pm_setup_stages` reads out of the release's own
+`setup_main` and writes to `w2-stages.txt` immediately before the install. For
+the source this plan was derived against, that sequence is `install_binary`
+(five executables), `register_skill`, `install_roles`, `write_install_state`,
+`check_path`, `configure_project` (returns immediately under the bare
+invocation), **`install_skills`** (the registered skill plus every `SKILL_REPOS`
+dependency, each with its `~/.claude` and `~/.codex` link) and `verify`.
+Duration is measured as `W2_end - W2_start`, not assumed sub-second.
+Default-PATH new spawn/route is withheld during `W2`; the absolute saved old
+pair remains the routing authority.
+
+Rollback commands:
